or the Apache License 2.0, at your option. FilmCraft, PhotoCraft, EffectCraft and SoundCraft pull in its crates at their own
revisions. DiscCraft uses directly craft-audio (its AC-3 encoder, which makes the transcoded soundtracks Dolby Digital;
revision 82062077bba679ba5236e2d1a391f02d1533cbab), craft-video (its H.264 encoder, formerly FilmCraft's
filmcraft-h264enc, which makes the HD Blu-ray video; the same revision; in tests also its MPEG-2 decoder), craft-media
(its MPEG-2 Systems, Matroska and MP4 readers, which take out video and audio that fit a disc as they are; the same
revision) and craft-ui (its docking, which arranges the panels and workspaces; revision 47107f660191de2f0b425569506f4daa4faadac9), and in tests
only craft-psd (PSD writer, revision eafb50aff3c6b1acc14dff53060157877e3e4fce). Its vendored Hayro crates are patched to
revision fe6b443acf3eccaf514064812e6e6bf24257652a in Cargo.toml.
